## Backend Testing Syntax & Common Pitfalls - Compilation Error Prevention

### Problem Pattern
Backend test compilation errors follow predictable patterns that waste significant development time:
- Namespace conflicts between custom services and third-party libraries
- Entity property and type mismatches 
- Incorrect mock setups for async/Task return types
- Database relationship configuration errors
- Authentication setup issues in integration tests

### Solution Pattern
**Follow established entity patterns and mock configurations to prevent compilation errors**

### Implementation

#### 1. Namespace Conflicts Resolution
**❌ WRONG - Ambiguous references:**
```csharp
// Causes conflict between GatherGrove.Application.Services.BillingService and Stripe.BillingService
private BillingService _billingService;
```

**✅ CORRECT - Fully qualified references:**
```csharp
private GatherGrove.Application.Services.BillingService _billingService;
private Mock<ILogger<GatherGrove.Application.Services.BillingService>> _mockLogger;
```

#### 2. Entity Property Patterns (GatherGrove Specific)
**❌ WRONG - Incorrect property names:**
```csharp
var user = new User {
    Id = Guid.NewGuid(),  // Wrong: Id is int, not Guid
    IsOnboardingCompleted = true  // Wrong: Property is OnboardingCompleted
};
```

**✅ CORRECT - Follow established entity structure:**
```csharp
var user = new User {
    // Don't set Id - it's auto-generated int identity
    FullName = "Test User",
    Email = "test@example.com", 
    PasswordHash = "hash",
    OnboardingCompleted = true  // Correct property name
};
```

#### 3. Mock Setup for Task Return Types
**❌ WRONG - Incorrect Task mock setup:**
```csharp
// Wrong for methods returning Task<bool>
_mockService.Setup(x => x.CancelSubscriptionAsync(It.IsAny<int>()))
    .ReturnsAsync(Task.FromResult(true));  // Double wrapping
```

**✅ CORRECT - Proper Task mock setup:**
```csharp
// For Task<bool> methods
_mockService.Setup(x => x.CancelSubscriptionAsync(It.IsAny<int>()))
    .ReturnsAsync(true);

// For Task methods (void async)
_mockService.Setup(x => x.ProcessWebhookAsync(It.IsAny<string>(), It.IsAny<string>()))
    .Returns(Task.CompletedTask);
```

#### 4. Database Test Setup Pattern
**MANDATORY pattern for in-memory database tests:**
```csharp
[SetUp]
public void Setup()
{
    var options = new DbContextOptionsBuilder<GatherGroveDbContext>()
        .UseInMemoryDatabase(databaseName: $"TestDb_{Guid.NewGuid()}")  // Unique per test
        .Options;
    
    _context = new GatherGroveDbContext(options);
    // Don't dispose here - dispose in TearDown
}

[TearDown] 
public void TearDown()
{
    _context.Dispose();  // Always dispose context
}
```

#### 5. Entity Relationship Setup (GatherGrove Pattern)
**✅ CORRECT - Follow established relationship pattern:**
```csharp
private async Task<(User user, Club club)> CreateTestUserAndClub(string tier = "Sprout")
{
    var user = new User {
        FullName = "Test User",
        Email = "test@example.com",
        PasswordHash = "hash", 
        OnboardingCompleted = true
        // Don't set Id - auto-generated
    };

    var club = new Club {
        Name = "Test Club",
        Tier = tier
        // Don't set Id - auto-generated
    };

    var clubAdmin = new ClubAdmin {
        User = user,  // Navigation property, not UserId
        Club = club   // Navigation property, not ClubId
    };

    _context.Users.Add(user);
    _context.Clubs.Add(club); 
    _context.ClubAdmins.Add(clubAdmin);
    await _context.SaveChangesAsync();

    return (user, club);
}
```

#### 6. Integration Test Authentication Setup
**Standard pattern for API integration tests:**
```csharp
private async Task<HttpClient> CreateAuthenticatedClientAsync(User user)
{
    var client = _factory.CreateClient();
    // Add authentication headers/JWT token setup here
    // Don't assume authentication is automatically handled
    return client;
}
```

#### 7. NUnit Assert.ThrowsAsync Pattern (GatherGrove Specific)
**❌ WRONG - Using await with Assert.ThrowsAsync:**
```csharp
// Causes "GetAwaiter not found" compilation errors
var ex = await Assert.ThrowsAsync<ArgumentException>(
    () => _service.SomeMethodAsync(invalidInput));
```

**✅ CORRECT - Follow established NUnit pattern:**
```csharp
// NO await - Assert.ThrowsAsync returns exception directly in this NUnit version
var ex = Assert.ThrowsAsync<ArgumentException>(
    () => _service.SomeMethodAsync(invalidInput));

Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain("expected error text"));
Assert.That(ex.ParamName, Is.EqualTo("parameterName")); // For ArgumentException
```

**Pattern Examples:**
```csharp
// ArgumentNullException
var ex = Assert.ThrowsAsync<ArgumentNullException>(
    () => _service.SomeMethodAsync(null!));
Assert.That(ex.ParamName, Is.EqualTo("request"));

// InvalidOperationException  
var ex = Assert.ThrowsAsync<InvalidOperationException>(
    () => _service.SomeMethodAsync(invalidState));
Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain("Invalid operation"));

// ArgumentException
var ex = Assert.ThrowsAsync<ArgumentException>(
    () => _service.SomeMethodAsync(invalidId));
Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain("not found"));
```

