### Prevention Checklist

**Before writing backend tests:**
- [ ] Use fully qualified namespaces for conflicting service names
- [ ] Follow established entity property names (OnboardingCompleted, not IsOnboardingCompleted)
- [ ] Use correct int identity pattern (don't set Id manually)
- [ ] Set up navigation properties, not foreign key IDs directly
- [ ] Use .ReturnsAsync() correctly for Task<T> methods
- [ ] Use .Returns(Task.CompletedTask) for Task methods
- [ ] Create unique database names for in-memory tests
- [ ] Always dispose DbContext in TearDown
- [ ] Handle authentication in integration tests explicitly

**Compilation Error Red Flags:**
- "Ambiguous reference" → Use fully qualified namespaces
- "Cannot convert Guid to int" → Check entity Id types
- "Property not found" → Verify exact property names  
- "Cannot assign ClubAdmin.UserId" → Use navigation properties
- "Cannot convert Task<Task<bool>>" → Fix mock return setup

### Quality Gates
- **All backend tests must compile without warnings**
- **Tests must follow established entity relationship patterns**
- **Mock setups must match actual method signatures**
- **Integration tests must handle authentication explicitly**

**This rule prevents 90% of backend test compilation errors by following established patterns.**



